  "instructions": [
    "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil for the spaghetti. Cook the spaghetti 1 minute less than the package time, until just tender.",
    "While the water heats, warm the olive oil in a deep 12-inch skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and carrots and cook 5 minutes, until soft.",
    "Add the mushrooms and cook 6 to 8 minutes, stirring often, until the liquid cooks off and they brown.",
    "Stir in the garlic, oregano, and basil. Cook 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the crushed tomatoes, lentils, water, salt, and pepper. Stir well.",
    "Simmer over medium-low heat for 12 minutes, stirring now and then, until the sauce is thick and clings to a spoon.",
    "Drain the spaghetti and toss it with half of the sauce, or serve the sauce on top.",
    "To freeze, cool the sauce completely and store it in airtight containers for up to 3 months. Reheat in a skillet over medium heat with a splash of water until hot."
  ],
